          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What cleaner should I use before pressure washing a patio?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the stain and material. A concrete and masonry cleaner handles most organic grime, a degreaser handles oil, and a masonry-safe rust remover handles rust. On natural stone, use products labelled stone-safe. Follow the label's dilution and dwell time."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often should a patio be pressure washed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most patios, once a year is enough, more often in damp, shaded areas where algae grows quickly. Regular sweeping and prompt rinsing of spills reduce how often you need a full clean, which is better for joints and softer surfaces."
          }
        }
